Niccolò

Any density estimate has an associated measure of uncertainty, probably a standard error. Given the pair of estimates and their standard errors, a statistical test can be conducted. In Buckland et al. (2001 <https://examples.distancesampling.org/differences/differences.html#ref-buckland2001>) [Sect. 3.6.5] methods are described to produce tests of significance based on t-test methods. A portion of that text is provided below

